The doors close behind me.
The S-Bahn pulls out.
I normally travel with the U-Bahn.
The U-Bahn often travels in a dark tunnel.
But this train travels above the streets.
I look out of the window.
The city passes by.
I see streets, trees and tall houses.
I rarely travel with the S-Bahn.
We stop at a few stations.
Many people get off and on.
After a few minutes I see the river.
The water is wide and blue.
The small shop is right by the river.
I look at the time on my mobile phone.
It is almost six o'clock.
The next station is the right one.
I must get out soon.
I take my backpack and go to the door.
